  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is a Table in HTML?</h2>
    <p>A table is used to show data in <b>rows and columns</b>. For example - a mark sheet, a price list, or a school time table.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> Student Marks Table, Product Price List, School Time Table — all are tables.</div>
    <p>There are 4 main tags for a table:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Work</th></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;table&gt;</td><td>Table</td><td>Creates the full table</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;tr&gt;</td><td>Table Row</td><td>Creates one row (one line)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;th&gt;</td><td>Table Heading</td><td>Heading - Bold + Center</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;td&gt;</td><td>Table Data</td><td>Normal data / cell</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>2. Basic Table - With 1 Heading Row + 1 Data Row</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;table</span> <span class="attr">border</span>=<span class="val">"1"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Name</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Marks</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">Ali</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">90</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/table&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><table class="demo-table"><tr><th>Name</th><th>Marks</th></tr><tr><td>Ali</td><td>90</td></tr></table></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Remember:</b> 1st &lt;tr&gt; = Heading Row (th) | 2nd &lt;tr&gt; = Data Row (td)</div>
    <h2>3. Full Table - 2 Students</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;table</span> <span class="attr">border</span>=<span class="val">"1"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Name</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Subject</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Marks</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">Ali</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">HTML</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">90</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">Ayesha</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">CSS</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">95</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/table&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><table class="demo-table"><tr><th>Name</th><th>Subject</th><th>Marks</th></tr><tr><td>Ali</td><td>HTML</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>Ayesha</td><td>CSS</td><td>95</td></tr></table></div>
    <h2>4. colspan - Merge Columns (Left to Right)</h2>
    <p><b>colspan</b> means one cell becomes as wide as 2 or more columns. Example: Make the main heading as wide as the full table.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;th</span> <span class="attr">colspan</span>=<span class="val">"3"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">My Class Result</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><table class="demo-table"><tr><th colspan="3">My Class Result</th></tr><tr><th>Name</th><th>Subject</th><th>Marks</th></tr><tr><td>Ali</td><td>HTML</td><td>90</td></tr></table></div>
    <h2>5. rowspan - Merge Rows (Top to Bottom)</h2>
    <p><b>rowspan</b> means one cell becomes as tall as 2 or more rows. Example: One name for 2 subjects.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;td</span> <span class="attr">rowspan</span>=<span class="val">"2"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Ali</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">HTML</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">CSS</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><table class="demo-table"><tr><th>Name</th><th>Subject</th></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">Ali</td><td>HTML</td></tr><tr><td>CSS</td></tr></table></div>
    <h2>6. Full Example - Price List</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;table</span> <span class="attr">border</span>=<span class="val">"1"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th</span> <span class="attr">colspan</span>=<span class="val">"3"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">My Shop Price List</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Product</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Price</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;th&gt;</span><span class="text">Stock</span><span class="tag">&lt;/th&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;tr&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">Shirt</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">1500</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;td&gt;</span><span class="text">Yes</span><span class="tag">&lt;/td&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/tr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/table&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Create a table with:</p>
    <p>1. Heading with <b>colspan="3"</b> = "My Result"<br>2. 2nd Row: Name | Subject | Marks<br>3. 3rd Row: Your Name | HTML | 100</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> table = Full table | tr = Row | th = Heading (Bold) | td = Data | colspan = Merge Columns | rowspan = Merge Rows | border="1" = To show border</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson7">Lesson 7 - Forms in HTML</a> to learn how to create forms.</p>
